  "summary": "York, Maine's selectboard voted to place a citizen's initiative on the November 3 ballot that would ban Flock automated license plate readers and require the town to remove existing cameras and cancel its Flock Safety contract. The article notes similar activity in Auburn, which has declined to renew its Flock contract, and South Portland, which removed its cameras earlier in the summer.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "York residents submitted a citizen's initiative to ban the cameras, which use artificial intelligence to scan and log license plate information on public roadways.",
      "paragraph_idx": 1
    },
    {
      "quote": "If it passes, the town must remove the cameras and cancel contracts with Flock Safety.",
      "paragraph_idx": 1
    },
    {
      "quote": "Some residents said the cameras, which are placed on Spur Road and Route 1 leading to the Maine Turnpike, violate their Fourth amendment rights.",
      "paragraph_idx": 2
    }
  ],
